criminal|lawbreaker|NOUN|person who commits a crime|A person who commits an act that the law treats as a crime.|người phạm tội|The novel follows a criminal who hides stolen paintings in a warehouse.|Cuốn tiểu thuyết kể về một người phạm tội giấu những bức tranh bị đánh cắp trong nhà kho.|Countable noun; plural criminals. A suspect is not necessarily a criminal.|0
criminal|related-to-crime|ADJECTIVE|relating to crime|Connected with crimes or the legal process used to deal with them.|thuộc về tội phạm hoặc luật hình sự|The students compared criminal law with the rules governing private contracts.|Các sinh viên so sánh luật hình sự với những quy định điều chỉnh hợp đồng tư.|Usually before a noun: criminal law, criminal investigation. Do not confuse criminal with civil.|1
homework|school-tasks-at-home|NOUN|schoolwork outside lessons|Tasks that a teacher expects students to complete outside their lessons.|bài tập về nhà|Lan finished her history homework before joining the family meal.|Lan làm xong bài tập lịch sử về nhà trước khi cùng gia đình dùng bữa.|Uncountable: some homework or a piece of homework, not a homework.|0
mouse|small-rodent|NOUN|small rodent|A small mammal with a pointed nose and a long thin tail.|con chuột nhỏ|A mouse slipped behind the cupboard when we opened the kitchen door.|Một con chuột nhỏ lủi ra sau tủ khi chúng tôi mở cửa bếp.|Countable; animal plural mice. Mouse names a small rodent, not every rat.|0
mouse|computer-control|NOUN|computer pointing device|A small device moved by hand to control a pointer on a computer screen.|chuột máy tính|Use the mouse to move the photograph into the empty box.|Dùng chuột máy tính để chuyển bức ảnh vào ô trống.|Countable; mice and mouses occur for devices. Click with the mouse; a touchpad is a different device.|1
register|enrol-or-record|VERB|enter an official record|To enter someone's details in an official record, or give your own details to join something.|đăng ký; ghi vào danh sách chính thức|Mai registered for the evening pottery course at the community centre.|Mai đăng ký khóa học làm gốm buổi tối tại trung tâm cộng đồng.|Register for a course; register with an organization; register something in someone's name. Both transitive and intransitive.|0
register|official-list|NOUN|official record of names|A record listing people or items for an official purpose.|sổ hoặc danh sách đăng ký|The caretaker checked the visitor register before closing the building.|Người trông coi kiểm tra sổ đăng ký khách trước khi đóng cửa tòa nhà.|Countable; a register of visitors. This record sense differs from a cash register or a language register.|1
seventy|number-70|NUMBER|number 70|The number that is ten more than sixty.|bảy mươi|Seventy chairs were arranged around the stage for the guests.|Bảy mươi chiếc ghế được xếp quanh sân khấu cho khách.|Cardinal number; seventy guests, not seventies guests. Seventieth is the ordinal form.|0
